1
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:08,900
There were men who burned with
fire to face the debt collectors.

2
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,360
Their chance comes once a year:
the year-end bonus.

3
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,350
But,

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,920
it was said that collecting
from that man was impossible.

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:18,771
This is

6
00:00:18,821 --> 00:00:23,200
the story of men who staked
their lives on the bonus battle.

7
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,140
When you watch TV, turn on the lights
and sit back from the screen, okay?

8
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:44,280
Anyone without money, come to my place!

9
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:49,060
I've got none either, but don't worry.

10
00:00:49,060 --> 00:01:02,960
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

11
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:19,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place!

12
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:24,540
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

13
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:31,960
Look, even the burning Akanel...

14
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:38,280
It'll all work out eventually.

15
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:41,560
You understand, right?

16
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,520
I understand, I understand.

17
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:47,480
Once you understand,
follow me without a word.

18
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,120
Talk.

19
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,360
Who are you guys?

20
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,460
We're the college wrestling team.

21
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:25,560
You're not getting away that easily.

22
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,880
That's dirty!
These guys are the opposition, after all.

23
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,900
Say whatever you like.

24
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:36,080
My salary.

25
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,480
Give it back, give it back.

26
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,020
I said give it back, you...

27
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,020
It hurts.

28
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:48,780
There, there, it's all right.

29
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:50,480
Turn on the light, quick.

30
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:52,980
There, there, there.

31
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:54,080
There, there, there.

32
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:58,380
Did your wife run out on you again?

33
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,740
She said she wouldn't come back until you paid off your debts,
the damn woman.

34
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,060
It happens every year, doesn't it?

35
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,120
It's a winter tradition, isn't it?

36
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:09,100
Now then, from here on,

37
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:14,020
we will hold the strategy meeting for
the 31st Ryotsu Kankichi Bonus Battle.

38
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,440
The footage just shown
was from seven years ago.

39
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:20,400
That's the footage of when we miraculously
managed to make a dash for Ryo-san's paycheck.

40
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:24,980
Back then,
we could afford to hire student part-timers

41
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,600
Ryo-san was off his guard, you know.

42
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:30,160
It was just a normal payday, after all.

43
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:33,740
I was toasting with my
wife that day, though.

44
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,980
But that actually made Ryo-san wary of us,

45
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:39,640
and we ended up failing to take the all-important bonus,
didn't we?

46
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:51,300
Over the past few years, we've pooled our wisdom and devised various strategies,
building new weapons on a small budget, desperately trying to

47
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,300
snatch the bonus,
but we've come up short every time.

48
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,660
But all of those ended in failure.

49
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:08,640
So while rewatching that video many times,
I suddenly came up with an idea.

50
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:12,860
that a simple plan might be
more effective against Ryo-san.

51
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:16,560
Now that you mention it, that's true.

52
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:18,860
We've been overthinking things all this time,
haven't we?

53
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:19,900
I see.

54
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,800
Cough, cough!
I've been saying that every year, you know!

55
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,620
Let's announce this year's strategy.

56
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:37,220
First-Strike Gacchari Strategy

57
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:40,240
Gacchari?

58
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,180
Bonus Struggle 6

59
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:50,400
No, no, no, no!

60
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:53,100
I absolutely cannot allow that!

61
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:55,380
Can't it just be one day?

62
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:57,380
No way!

63
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,720
Damn it, that chief and his stubbornness!

64
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,320
So it really is you, Ryo-sama.

65
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,860
I flew right over when I heard your voice.

66
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:08,520
Maria

67
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:11,120
What business did you have with the chief?

68
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:15,620
I tried to get my bonus paid one day early,
but he turned me down.

69
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:17,280
Come on, why?

70
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:21,240
Lend me some money, because when payday comes,
the debt collectors will swarm in on us.

71
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:23,260
I was planning to outsmart them.

72
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,360
Wouldn't it be better to
pay back your debts quickly?

73
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,800
What is this computer?

74
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:33,000
Since they said they bought new computers,

75
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,580
you're going to throw
the old ones away, right?

76
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,760
What a waste.

77
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,780
Isn't there a single one that still works?

78
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,020
No good.

79
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,620
They're all too old.

80
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:44,700
Even if we take them to a secondhand shop,
they're all the kind that won't sell.

81
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,900
I've never seen computers
this ancient before.

82
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:00,160
This is the computer for managing salaries.

83
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:06,600
The data's still sitting right there,
you know.

84
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,620
How careless.

85
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,280
So that guy gets this much?

86
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,780
Let's see, how about me...

87
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,080
Found it.

88
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,360
The one on the far
right is the bonus, right?

89
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,680
Compared to my classmates...

90
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,240
That's low. Not fair.

91
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:27,555
1, 10, 100, 1,000, 100 million!?

92
00:06:27,605 --> 00:06:28,560
Lord Ryo!

93
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:31,660
It's a computer we're throwing out anyway.
Just for fun, just for fun.

94
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:35,160
True enough. In that case,
I'll take about two million as well.

95
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,980
What a modest one you are.

96
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:39,960
How about this?

97
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,080
Thank you so much!

98
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,620
Right, I'll change the others' bonuses too.

99
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,300
It's Terai.

100
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:54,180
He's got a house loan and suffers
through commuting hell every day.

101
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:58,500
Since he's so pitiful,
I'll give him about ten million.

102
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,980
As expected of you, Ryo-sama, so kind.

103
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:03,740
Next...

104
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:05,380
The Chief?

105
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:09,220
The Chief turned down my offer earlier,
after all.

106
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,520
I'll knock off two digits.

107
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:15,700
Thirty thousand and twenty-five yen...
that should be enough for this.

108
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,520
Next is Reiko

109
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,920
For Reiko,
let's make it a nice-looking 5 yen,

110
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,480
5 yen it is.

111
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,560
Lovely.

112
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,700
Next is Keiichi Nakagawa.

113
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:28,960
Nakagawa loves being
number one at everything, so

114
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,560
It's 1 yen.

115
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:35,940
We'll cut everyone else's pay down,
one after another.

116
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,980
Sugimura gets 30 yen.

117
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,600
Pepp gets 100 yen.

118
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,000
Is 10 yen good enough?

119
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,760
Wakana gets 15 yen.

120
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,040
The chief

121
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:51,700
Right, everyone says the chief is
the model of a police officer, so

122
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:59,620
110 yen. Just what you'd expect from Chief Ohara.
Even his bonus is a figure fit for a police officer.

123
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:01,660
What's this about my bonus?

124
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:02,120
Gulp!

125
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,360
Chief!

126
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:09,260
Chief! What a coincidence
running into you here.

127
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:09,420
Hey.

128
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:12,580
What do you mean, coincidence?

129
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:13,600
You're on duty, aren't you?

130
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,000
What are you doing here, goofing off?

131
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,640
I was just about to head back.

132
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:20,480
Well then, Ryo-san, see you later.

133
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,000
Well, I'll be taking my leave too.

134
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,640
You're supposed to be at the police box,
aren't you?

135
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,420
Ow ow!

136
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:28,720
Okay, okay, just let go of me.

137
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:31,360
Then I'll take this.

138
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,320
Thanks.

139
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,380
Yeah.

140
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:38,280
Wait a second.

141
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:45,220
We're using it. Who left this here?
Hey, put this one inside too.

142
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:45,920
Yes.

143
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:53,260
Send the bonus data to the bank. Yes.

144
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,980
Transmission complete.
Thanks for your hard work.

145
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,640
W-what?
The bonuses aren't out yet, you know!

146
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,500
I know that perfectly well.

147
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,820
Then why?

148
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:26,360
Wh-what are you doing, Puramo-yan!

149
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:29,180
It's to recover the debts you owe me.

150
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,380
I told you there's no bonus yet, didn't I?

151
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:36,300
So until the bonus comes out,
I'm going to stick with you like this.

152
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,080
What?

153
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,180
Once I thought of it, it was easy.

154
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:43,700
If you try to catch him on bonus day,
he'll just run away.

155
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,280
Then just catch him before that.

156
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:47,180
This is it!

157
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,380
Fair and square!

158
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:49,940
Operation Disappointment Showdown.

159
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:53,680
Thinking you can get away with this...

160
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,360
Chief Ohara has already
given his permission.

161
00:09:56,360 --> 00:10:00,040
Until the bonus comes out,
you and I are one and the same.

162
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,340
No way.

163
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:16,660
I couldn't get away.

164
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,820
Thanks for waiting for me, everyone.

165
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:21,840
Good work, Oramu-ya.

166
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,700
Really, thanks for your hard work.

167
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,780
You really are a man, you know.

168
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:28,600
Save your tears until you've got the bonus.

169
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,920
Check that the bonus has
actually been deposited.

170
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:46,880
Anyway, the bonus is always
about the same every year.

171
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:52,960
So zeros make 100, that means

172
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,200
One million.

173
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:54,380
What?

174
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:57,020
100 million yen

175
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:59,360
Ryo-san, what on earth did you do?

176
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,760
What is this money?

177
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:03,440
I don't know. I don't understand it either.

178
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,980
Come to think of it,
I read about this in the newspaper.

179
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:12,180
about a man who became the richest man in the world for a moment
Translation>
because of a bank's mistake.

180
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,920
So in my case too, because of a bank error,

181
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,680
maybe

182
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,880
I withdraw the entire deposit
before the bank notices.

183
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,060
I can only withdraw 1 million.

184
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:24,480
But if it's the bank's mistake,

185
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,960
the one who made the mistake is at fault.

186
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:28,640
Once money enters my account, it's mine.

187
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:33,800
Ryotsu-sama.

188
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:34,980
Yes.

189
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,700
Thank you for waiting.

190
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,840
So this is 100 million.

191
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,560
It's not as bulky as I expected.

192
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:45,740
Exchange it all for 2,000-yen bills.

193
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:47,300
Yes.

194
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,220
Here you go.

195
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:57,100
Now I'm finally starting to feel rich.

196
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,560
This is 100 million?

197
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,420
I've never seen this much money before.

198
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,660
That's why you can't trust machines.

199
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,760
I think so too.

200
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:17,680
But is it really alright?
Taking it for yourself like that?

201
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,980
I have nothing to be ashamed of.

202
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:23,717
It was deposited in my account,
so I'll use it.

203
00:12:23,767 --> 00:12:24,940
That's all there is to it.

204
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:28,230
Now, let's have those
debtors or whoever pay up.

205
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,680
I'll make them pay it back
with plenty of interest.

206
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:38,220
Is that all? Compared to 100 million,
it's just pocket change.

207
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:42,260
By the way, this is 200,000 yen.
That's a hundred 2,000-yen bills.

208
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:47,174
There's no need to keep this on forever,
is there?

209
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:49,280
I'm telling you I'll pay.

210
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:49,900
But...

211
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:53,500
Do you think I'd make a fuss
over such a measly sum now?

212
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,500
Fair enough.

213
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:57,880
Hey, old lady, the key.

214
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:58,540
Here you go.

215
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,920
That's a relief.

216
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:05,660
Being stuck to that Pura-Mo
the whole time was really rough.

217
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,920
The feeling's mutual.

218
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:09,400
Now, first up is the Tsurukame Dog.

219
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,080
Yes.

220
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:12,780
Keep the change.

221
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:13,760
Keep it.

222
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:28,560
Ah, aah!

223
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:33,180
Ah, aah!

224
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,260
Ah, aah!

225
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:34,660
Ah, aah!

226
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,000
Whoa!

227
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,020
Ryo-san

228
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:42,860
What's wrong?

229
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:46,620
N-no, my hand just won't let go of it!

230
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:50,580
Maybe it's like this
every year at this time,

231
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,640
Ryo-san has lived his whole life
running from debt collectors.

232
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:57,900
This unimaginable struggle has,
without him knowing,

233
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,400
taught Ryo-san's body to protect his bonus

234
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:03,360
by instilling in it a self-defense instinct.

235
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:08,840
That's why his body refuses to pay us back.

236
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:12,500
Ryo-san's body is now incapable
of paying off his debts.

237
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,940
Everyone, quick,
take back your share of the debt!

238
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,600
My body just moves on its own.

239
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,220
Don't flinch! Everyone, charge at once!

240
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:33,940
Then I'll pay off my
debts with my next bonus.

241
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:37,200
Wait!

242
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,080
What is this?

243
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:43,080
Why is my bonus only 5 yen?

244
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:44,960
Mine's only 1 yen!

245
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,380
110 yen? What kind of joke is this!

246
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:52,760
How much did Terai get?
Was it another joke of an amount?

247
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:56,940
W-well, I got 10 million yen...

248
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:01,960
Ryo-sama!

249
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,860
Maria-chan

250
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:08,900
I think Ryo-san went to the bank
with the shopping district people.

251
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:12,540
Aaahhh!

252
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:16,140
W-well, then it might be too late already.

253
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,400
What's wrong?

254
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,254
Nakagawa,

255
00:15:19,304 --> 00:15:22,880
Wasn't your bonus just one yen, Nakagawa?

256
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:23,900
Y-yes.

257
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:27,360
Reiko's was five yen. How do you know that?

258
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:30,820
And Chief Ohara's was 110 yen, I think.

259
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:33,180
That's right. But how do you know?

260
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:34,372
Earlier,

261
00:15:34,422 --> 00:15:38,940
Ryo-sama jokingly typed into the
computer that was sitting in the hallway.

262
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,640
It's 110 yen.

263
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:44,940
That's when it was.

264
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:50,500
It seems that data was accidentally
sent to the bank by mistake.

265
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:55,680
We noticed just now and
contacted the bank right away, but

266
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,380
No, I'll take it.

267
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,280
Yes, Kameari Park police box.

268
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,220
Yeah, it's me. How did it go?

269
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:30,160
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

270
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:33,560
The total bonus amount for the whole
division has already been decided.

271
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:37,000
So unless we get the bonus back from Ryotsu,

272
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,620
we won't be able to
receive our proper bonuses.

273
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:44,800
Whatever it takes, catch Ryotsu.

274
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:53,180
Emergency order, emergency order.

275
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:54,980
Attention, all section chiefs.

276
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:57,580
Immediately secure Senior Constable Ryotsu.

277
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,500
Our bonuses

278
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:06,600
are in the hands of Senior
Constable Kankichi Ryotsu.

279
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,480
Repeat.

280
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,920
Senior Constable Ryotsu

281
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:11,180
is on the move with everyone's bonuses.

282
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,140
Find him.

283
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,680
Secure him properly.

284
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,320
Damn, these stacks of cash are too heavy!

285
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,480
I shouldn't have gone and
changed it all to 2,000-yen bills.

286
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:43,680
Thank goodness.

287
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,500
Hey, Volvo Sagonji!

288
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:48,060
Give back the money!

289
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:53,700
I don't owe you guys any debts, do I?

290
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:00,220
Why are those guys chasing me too?

291
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:05,740
Watch out, mister!

292
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:07,040
Step on it!

293
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,500
Damn it, just drive anywhere, and hurry!

294
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,040
I'll pay you whatever you want!

295
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:14,780
Yes.

296
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:18,360
Damn it!

297
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,460
This is Volvo, Ryotsu spotted!

298
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:24,520
He's fleeing by taxi toward Ueno right now.

299
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,020
Attention all officers.

300
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:30,240
Senior Constable Kankichi
Ryotsu is heading toward Ueno.

301
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:33,100
All officers, rush to Ueno!

302
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:33,840
Repeat, over.

303
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,000
Bravoya, where are you going?

304
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:39,020
Leave Ryo-san's movement patterns to me.

305
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:40,920
We'll get ahead of him.

306
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:43,720
Roger.

307
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,180
Right, we'll make a run for it by train!

308
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:52,820
That's far enough!

309
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:57,940
Pocketing the big money and
running off till the heat dies down

310
00:18:57,940 --> 00:19:01,200
We know all of Ryo-san's moves.

311
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:04,160
Come on, give up, Ryo-san!

312
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,740
That's right.

313
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:08,200
Grrah!

314
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,260
Grrah!

315
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,360
Everyone, it's money!

316
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:15,300
Damn! Quick, get Ryo-san...

317
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:17,360
Whoa!

318
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:23,140
Full speed ahead!

319
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,520
Ryo-san's getting away!

320
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:26,420
Ugh!

321
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:27,160
Listen up!

322
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:29,520
Keep it!

323
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,900
Shortly arriving at Track 16,

324
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:34,760
the special train will be departing.

325
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,640
Here it is!

326
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,480
Whoa! S-sorry!

327
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:41,080
This is a chartered wedding train, you know.

328
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,000
Except for family and friends,

329
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,460
from this moment on, we're friends!

330
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:46,040
It's my principle! Keep it!

331
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,500
Next station!

332
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:11,580
The police are chasing Ryo-san
with everything they've got!

333
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:14,960
Wasn't that money a bit dangerous?

334
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,340
It doesn't matter what
kind of money that is!

335
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:20,100
We're getting back what we're owed.

336
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:21,500
That's all there is to it.

337
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,960
Damn! They cut us off!

338
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:32,920
Yes!

339
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,740
Yes!

340
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,020
Yes!

341
00:20:44,940 --> 00:20:45,720
What the hell!

342
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:47,960
He's not here!

343
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:49,240
There he is!

344
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:51,620
Scary!

345
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,260
That's the fare for going past your stop!

346
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:58,180
Damn it! Why are the cops chasing me too!

347
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,820
Yes!

348
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,020
Damn it!

349
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:08,360
Everyone, take it!

350
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,620
Oh my god!

351
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:17,720
Police! Please move aside!

352
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,160
Pervert!

353
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:20,720
Maybe I'll just take it...

354
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:24,440
If you're going to pull something like this,
pay back your debts!

355
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:26,720
This is our money!

356
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,700
Hurry up and go!

357
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:39,240
Step on it and go faster!

358
00:21:40,160 --> 00:21:41,240
I've chartered you for today.

359
00:21:42,240 --> 00:21:43,480
Let me ride along too!

360
00:21:44,380 --> 00:21:45,620
Give it the whip!

361
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:48,860
This is so easy, so easy!

362
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:54,000
Gogoro?

363
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,300
What is this? I love it!

364
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:03,560
That'll be enough!

365
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:05,420
But...

366
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:07,560
Then how about this?

367
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:10,340
I have evasion, so...

368
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:17,760
Then how about this?

369
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:21,400
With this much, you can't complain, right?

370
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:22,880
Go!

371
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:23,300
Go!

372
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:32,600
Aaaaah!

373
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:33,880
Aaaaah!

374
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:40,380
They won't be able to follow me this far.

375
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:43,620
Now, let me take a good look at my bonus,

376
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:47,480
but first, I'll get my debts paid back.

377
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,580
Plamoya! Why are you here?

378
00:22:49,580 --> 00:22:53,140
I said I had Ryo-san's
moves all figured out!

379
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:55,060
I won't hand over the bonus!

380
00:22:55,060 --> 00:22:56,860
There's nowhere to run! Give up!

381
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,740
Forget it!

382
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,860
I can't take this anymore!

383
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:01,860
I'm going to die!

384
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,140
W-why?

385
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:10,560
No way, did he spend it all on his getaway?

386
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,100
There's no other explanation.

387
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,980
Well, at least we've got this much.

388
00:23:15,980 --> 00:23:17,260
This is mine!

389
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:19,200
It's all mine, just like this!

390
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:20,140
He just came out of there!

391
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,280
Alright!

392
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,380
Bonus secured!

393
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:59,500
Aww! Why does it always end up like this?!

394
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:24,540
I walked while looking back,

395
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:27,180
led along by a child's hand.

396
00:24:28,240 --> 00:24:34,340
That strange feeling I had back then,

397
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:39,620
so on the arcade's guide tiles,

398
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,400
I tried walking only on the black parts.

399
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

400
00:24:54,640 --> 00:25:01,000
Pompous-faced politicians and the blue-haired
aunties who are a thorn in your side too

401
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:06,580
Why don't you turn that corner over there

402
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:11,780
You can meet everyone, everyone

403
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:12,940
Don't go

404
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:16,220
That's Kameari over there

405
00:25:17,540 --> 00:25:19,700
Well, surely it's Kameari

406
00:25:19,700 --> 00:25:24,920
Everyone, come on over to our town

407
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:26,520
Thank you

408
00:25:29,300 --> 00:25:30,100
Damn it

409
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:34,200
We got the chief photographed while he was
doing his hanging scroll thing in seventh place

410
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:37,680
And the place I ended up at
to get it back is this company

411
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:40,120
Is it a scam, a purse snatching, or a lure?

412
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:43,893
Next time,

413
00:25:43,943 --> 00:25:47,800
Bottomless Thieves Inc.! See you then!

